§14's same-site rule reconstructs the supersession relation downstream, from
(src, call line, edge_type, callee name key) over the post-dedup graph. That
reconstruction cannot tell a REFINEMENT of a stub from a COLLISION with an
unrelated call sharing the line and short name -- which is what produced Open
question 4's 45 false demotions. The pass that consumed the stub already knows
which one, and Edge.derived_from is where it says so.

A resolved edge whose derived_from names an unresolved edge now demotes that
edge: no key, no line, no candidate set, no ambiguity to refuse. It runs before
the same-site rule and stamps the same two meta keys, which that rule then
skips, so one stub is halved once however many rules reach it -- otherwise the
declared 0.5 factor would be a lie. It is not gated on two anchored producers:
a stated derivation needs no second observer.

derived_from was populated and said nothing. Measured before this change:
48,879 edges carried it, 100.0% were exactly [edge.src, edge.dst], and ZERO
referenced an edge -- WI-ratun's finding, reproduced on every linker that
populates the field. The two recovery passes now record what they consumed:
inherited_calls names the unresolved edge plus the class its walk started
from, method_call_recovery the unresolved call plus the class-hint edge.

THE PERMISSION IS DECLARED PER PASS AND GRANTED ON MEASUREMENT.
RegisteredLinker.supersedes_consumed_stub defaults to False, because demoting
a stub ranks a producer's positive answer below the consuming pass's own and a
pass that is wrong a quarter of the time buries the right answer a quarter of
the time -- with a superseded_by stamp inviting the consumer to trust it. This
is §5's citation discipline applied to a different permission; the table is
docs/audits/0020.

  GRANTED  inherited-calls-linker       70/70 audited correct, 329/329
                                        consistent with the inheritance graph
  REFUSED  method-call-recovery-linker  16 of 64 wrong

The refusal is measured, not asserted: disambiguation_fallback -- the one
shipped quality signal -- is set on 5 of the 16 wrong and 13 of the 48 right,
so gating on it would discard 28% of the wrong and 27% of the right. There is
nothing to condition on, so the grant is refused rather than conditioned on a
number with no derivation. That pass still stamps its consumed edge; the
provenance is true, the demotion is not licensed.

Measured on a single-backend Python self-survey of this repository:

  demotions                       0 -> 329  (all inherited-calls-linker)
  edges with an edge reference
  in derived_from                 0 -> 393  (first in the corpus)
  inherited-calls-linker edges  329 -> 329
  method-call-recovery edges     64 ->  64

NOT DONE: WI-latup's wider sweep. The other ~56 linker files still write their
edge's own [src, dst]. Only the two passes with a consumer for the field were
changed; each remaining site needs a judgement about what its real upstream
evidence is, nothing would go red if I got one wrong, and it does not belong in
a PR about a supersession rule. WI-latup stays open with the measurement.

